# Whatever happens in Russian: что бы ни, как ни, где бы ни
subtitle: "Что бы ни, где бы ни, как ни: how to say whatever happens and however hard it is in Russian, on an August evening by the Neva."
tags: ["russian","что бы ни","как ни","concessive clauses","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/concessive","vocabulary/feelings"]
thumb: "band \"Whatever happens\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"The thing is… in Russian: дело в том, что; о том, чтобы","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/192-russian-the-thing-is.cast"}

